[agent] The diverging feature is **f2**.
[agent] ## How I found it
[agent] All computation ran platform-side. I ingested both CSVs as Hopsworks feature groups (`training_sample_1`, `serving_log_1`, keyed on `entity_id`), then joined them on `entity_id` over the 200 shared entities using the platform's Trino engine (Delta catalog) and computed per-feature divergence:
[agent] | feature | mean abs diff | correlation |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | f1 | 0.0 | 1.000 |
[agent] | **f2** | **7.19** | **0.926** |
[agent] | f3 | 0.0 | 1.000 |
[agent] | f4 | 0.0 | 1.000 |
[agent] | f5 | 0.0 | 1.000 |
[agent] f1/f3/f4/f5 match exactly; only **f2** diverges.
[agent] ## Cause
[agent] I characterized the relationship platform-side and found it's exact: **`f2_training = ln(1 + f2_serving)`** (log1p), with `corr(s.f2, exp(t.f2)) = 1.0` and max residual ~5e-7. So the training pipeline applies a `log1p` transform to `f2`, while the online service serves the **raw, un-transformed** value (equivalently, serving = `expm1(training)`). The fix is to apply the same `log1p` on the serving path — ideally as a feature-view-attached transformation so both paths share one definition.
